{
  "42": {
    "document_id": "42",
    "label": "1",
    "explanation": "Lott and Collins announce that their negotiated agreement 'resulted in the following provisions being included in the Collins-Lieberman legislation.' Under clarification (3), claims that the senator's negotiated language was included in legislation count as credit-claiming; the release explicitly claims shared responsibility for provisions reshaping FEMA being incorporated into the bill."
  },
  "714": {
    "document_id": "714",
    "label": "1",
    "explanation": "Although much of the column is informational about the U.S. Marshals Service, the senator explicitly states, 'I helped secure more than $3 billion in the fiscal year 2006 Homeland Security appropriations bill for ICE's domestic enforcement efforts, as well as funding for 250 additional criminal investigators.' This is a direct claim of responsibility for delivered federal funds, squarely within clarification (2) ('I helped secure')."
  },
  "794": {
    "document_id": "794",
    "label": "1",
    "explanation": "Bond touts that 'the new federal highway bill, which Bond co-authored, is providing Missouri with much-needed resources, including $1 billion in new money — more than $4 billion in total funding.' This claims authorship responsibility for enacted legislation delivering concrete funds to his state, falling under clarifications (2), (3), and (5) (record of enacted legislation benefiting a constituency)."
  },
  "805": {
    "document_id": "805",
    "label": "1",
    "explanation": "Shelby announces that the Department of Homeland Security 'will release $3,510 to the Homewood Fire Department' through the Assistance to Firefighters Grant Program. Under clarification (1), announcing that federal grant money is flowing to a community in the senator's state counts as credit-claiming even without an explicit 'I secured,' because the announcement associates the senator with delivery of the benefit."
  },
  "1257": {
    "document_id": "1257",
    "label": "1",
    "explanation": "DeWine announces a $105,550 grant to the Parma Fire Department and explicitly claims responsibility: he 'wrote and passed the FIRE Act,' 'helped secure approximately $650 million' for it, and passed an updated version. This is textbook credit-claiming under clarifications (1) and (2)—announcing funds flowing to his state plus explicit claims of authorship and securing funds."
  },
  "1325": {
    "document_id": "1325",
    "label": "0",
    "explanation": "Dole's floor statement criticizes Democrats' filibuster of judicial nominees and defends the 'constitutional option.' It is entirely an issue-position statement and criticism of opponents, with no assertion of responsibility for any delivered benefit. Per the negative clarification (statements of issue positions; criticism of opponents), this is not credit-claiming."
  },
  "1749": {
    "document_id": "1749",
    "label": "0",
    "explanation": "Hutchison merely 'signed on as an original cosponsor' of the Veterans Housing Benefits Enhancement Act, which was just introduced. The negative clarification expressly excludes 'merely introducing or cosponsoring a bill' as advocacy regarding pending proposals with no delivered result. No benefit has been delivered and no past achievement is touted."
  },
  "1897": {
    "document_id": "1897",
    "label": "0",
    "explanation": "Martinez states his position on the pending Pombo OCS bill—applauding Congressman Putnam's efforts, objecting to the inadequate buffer, and threatening a filibuster. This is an issue position on pending legislation with no delivered benefit and no claim of causal responsibility for an outcome; it fits the negative clarifications (issue positions; applauding another actor's efforts without claiming credit)."
  },
  "1927": {
    "document_id": "1927",
    "label": "1",
    "explanation": "Snowe announces that $8.1 million for the Portsmouth Naval Shipyard 'was requested by Snowe and Sen. Collins' and is included in an appropriations bill that 'passed the Senate today,' along with $23.8 billion in veterans funding she supported and requested via letter to appropriators. This matches clarifications (1), (2), and (3): announcing federal funds flowing to her state, claiming personal responsibility ('requested by Snowe'), and noting the bill passed a chamber."
  },
  "2335": {
    "document_id": "2335",
    "label": "1",
    "explanation": "While the release primarily announces an essay contest honoring fathers (an event, ordinarily not credit-claiming), it includes substantive passages touting Bayh's record: 'One of Senator Bayh's first pieces of legislation... was the Responsible Fatherhood Act, parts of which were signed into law by President Bush,' and that as governor he 'more than doubled the amount of money collected for child support payments.' Under clarifications (3) and (5), claims that his legislation was enacted and passages touting delivered outcomes, even packaged with an event, constitute credit-claiming. This distinguishes it from the Allard town-meeting negative example, which contained no such achievement claims."
  },
  "2869": {
    "document_id": "2869",
    "label": "0",
    "explanation": "Jeffords' statement simply explains why he voted for the Kerry and Levin amendments on Iraq and criticizes the Administration's lack of an exit strategy. Per the negative clarification, explanations of votes and statements of issue positions are not credit-claiming; no benefit delivered by Jeffords is asserted."
  },
  "3252": {
    "document_id": "3252",
    "label": "1",
    "explanation": "The headline and text announce that the 'Senate Adopts Nelson Amendment'—'his amendment... passed on a bipartisan vote of 72 to 26' as part of the FY2006 Agriculture Appropriations bill. Under clarification (3), claims that the senator's amendment was adopted (passed at any stage) are credit-claiming, and Nelson frames it as 'a victory for Nebraska's ranchers.'"
  },
  "4022": {
    "document_id": "4022",
    "label": "0",
    "explanation": "Kennedy's floor statement introduces a 'Medicare for All' bill, catalogs health-care problems, and criticizes the Bush administration and Republicans. It is advocacy for a new proposal plus criticism of opponents, with no delivered benefit claimed. Under the negative clarification (merely introducing a bill; issue positions; criticism of the administration), this is not credit-claiming."
  },
  "4122": {
    "document_id": "4122",
    "label": "1",
    "explanation": "Although framed around a hearing announcement, the release claims the Subcommittee's oversight produced concrete results: 'Due to the Subcommittee's oversight collections from delinquent Defense contractors skyrocketed by 4,415%... to $31 million in 2006 alone,' and levies 'raking in an additional $122 million in back taxes.' Clarification (4) expressly includes claims that the senator's oversight or investigation produced concrete results such as funds recouped."
  },
  "4184": {
    "document_id": "4184",
    "label": "0",
    "explanation": "Kyl 'co-sponsored legislation' and offered an amendment to the Budget Resolution that 'calls for' $352 million for 2,000 new Border Patrol agents, but there is no indication the amendment was adopted or any funds delivered. Under the negative clarification, merely co-sponsoring or offering a pending proposal with no delivered result is not credit-claiming."
  },
  "4207": {
    "document_id": "4207",
    "label": "1",
    "explanation": "The release is mainly advocacy (a letter urging Secretary Chertoff to consider the IBWC levee proposal), which alone would not qualify. However, it also touts Cornyn's record: he 'added an amendment to the Department of State and Foreign Operations Appropriations bill that required the IBWC... to report to Congress,' an adopted provision, on behalf of South Texas counties. Under clarifications (3) and (5), claims that the senator's amendment was adopted and passages touting his enacted legislative efforts for a constituency constitute credit-claiming even when packaged with new advocacy. I acknowledge some ambiguity since the report requirement is a modest benefit, but the codebook's inclusion of adopted amendments is categorical."
  },
  "4295": {
    "document_id": "4295",
    "label": "1",
    "explanation": "Although the release announces newly introduced legislation (which alone would be excluded as mere introduction), it substantively touts Murkowski's past delivered benefit: 'she helped win a two-year change in the Economic Growth Reconciliation Act... that provided the state with an additional $34.11 million above the traditional Medicaid formula amount.' Under clarification (5), a passage touting the senator's record of delivered benefits for her state, even packaged with a new proposal, is credit-claiming."
  },
  "4508": {
    "document_id": "4508",
    "label": "1",
    "explanation": "Lott announces that FEMA is moving roughly 300 travel trailers and 100 mobile homes to South Mississippi for Katrina victims, and the release explicitly states the move 'follows the Senator's Monday appeal to President Bush.' This is both an announcement of benefits flowing to his state (clarification 1) and a claim that his personal intervention produced the delivered result (clarification 4)."
  },
  "4677": {
    "document_id": "4677",
    "label": "0",
    "explanation": "The release describes Hutchison's questions at a subcommittee hearing, her receiving assurances that BRAC is on schedule, and her support for the Army's 'Grow the Force' request. She says she is 'encouraged to see $18 million in the emergency supplemental for facilities at Fort Hood' but claims no causal role in securing it—this is merely applauding/commenting on pending budget items and general expressions of support ('I have supported increasing the Army's end strength'), which the negative clarification excludes (hearing announcements; welcoming without claiming a causal role; general support not tied to a specific delivered benefit)."
  },
  "4774": {
    "document_id": "4774",
    "label": "1",
    "explanation": "While Bayh urges conferees to retain his provision (advocacy on a pending matter), the release also states that 'the Senate unanimously approved an amendment offered by Senators Bayh and Richard Durbin' to end the Patriot Penalty. Under clarification (3), claims that the senator's amendment was adopted or passed at any stage count as credit-claiming; the Senate's approval of his amendment is a delivered legislative result he claims as his own."
  }
}

{
  "157": {
    "document_id": "157",
    "label": "0",
    "explanation": "The release is only a bare notice that the Small Business Committee Chair held a markup on venture capital and education bills, with no substantive content. The codebook's negative clarification expressly excludes 'announcements of town meetings, hearings, or markups.' No benefit is announced and no responsibility is claimed."
  },
  "189": {
    "document_id": "189",
    "label": "0",
    "explanation": "Leahy's statement is advocacy at a hearing for allowing cameras in federal courts, coupled with criticism of the Bush administration's secrecy policies. He notes he has cosponsored pending bills (Sunshine in the Courtroom Act, Televising Supreme Court Proceedings Act), but the negative clarification expressly excludes 'merely introducing or cosponsoring a bill' and 'advocacy, urging, or demands regarding pending proposals with no delivered result.' No delivered benefit or adopted provision is claimed."
  },
  "744": {
    "document_id": "744",
    "label": "0",
    "explanation": "Allard's release reports that he sent a letter to the Acting Secretary of the Air Force requesting clear religious expression guidelines at the Academy. This is a request/urging directed at a pending matter with no delivered result, which the negative clarification excludes ('advocacy, urging, or demands regarding pending proposals with no delivered result'). No agency action or benefit is announced."
  },
  "873": {
    "document_id": "873",
    "label": "1",
    "explanation": "The release announces a concrete, delivered benefit\u2014Medicare's confirmation that hurricane-affected Louisiana seniors can enroll in Part D through December 31, 2006 without penalty\u2014and explicitly ties it to Landrieu's advocacy: the headline says the 'Administrator finally responds to Sen. Landrieu's letter,' and the text states the testimony 'responds to urgent calls for clarification made by' Landrieu, who wrote to Dr. McClellan. This fits clarification (4): claims that the senator's letters or advocacy produced concrete results (an agency decision following their request)."
  },
  "964": {
    "document_id": "964",
    "label": "0",
    "explanation": "Landrieu and Kerry 'call for' local contracts in Katrina/Rita rebuilding and write the SBA to speed up loss verification. This is advocacy and urging directed at pending matters with no delivered result, which the negative clarification expressly excludes. No benefit is announced and no outcome is claimed to have resulted from their actions."
  },
  "1043": {
    "document_id": "1043",
    "label": "1",
    "explanation": "The release announces a concrete federal benefit flowing to Ohio constituents\u2014a $78,046 grant to the Troy Township Fire Department\u2014and explicitly claims DeWine's responsibility: he 'wrote and passed the FIRE Act,' 'helped secure $650 million' for it, and passed an updated version. This squarely fits clarification (1) (announcing federal money flowing to the state) and (2) (explicit claims of responsibility such as authoring legislation and securing funds), mirroring the Talent positive example."
  },
  "1139": {
    "document_id": "1139",
    "label": "0",
    "explanation": "This is a condolence statement on the death of Rep. Charlie Norwood, expressing sympathy and hope that Congress continues his legacy. The negative clarification expressly excludes 'condolences, tributes, and remembrances.' No benefit is announced and no credit is claimed for any delivered outcome."
  },
  "1610": {
    "document_id": "1610",
    "label": "0",
    "explanation": "Reid's remarks at the CHIP enrollment ceremony credit others (Baucus, Rockefeller, Grassley, Hatch) for the bipartisan bill and criticize the President for threatening a veto, urging him to sign. Reid asserts no personal responsibility for any delivered benefit, and the bill has not been enacted\u2014it faces a veto threat. This is a position statement/advocacy, which the negative clarification excludes ('statements of issue positions'; 'criticism of the administration')."
  },
  "1736": {
    "document_id": "1736",
    "label": "0",
    "explanation": "The release's subject is Domenici's request for an expedited hearing and markup on the Livestock Assistance Act, a bill he cosponsored\u2014exactly the 'advocacy, urging, or demands regarding pending proposals with no delivered result (including merely introducing or cosponsoring a bill)' that the negative clarification excludes. A closing paragraph notes that after Domenici and others asked USDA and the President to approve any New Mexico emergency aid request, USDA announced low-interest emergency loan eligibility in 20 counties. I judged this insufficient for credit-claiming: the linkage is implied only by juxtaposition (unlike the Lott example's explicit 'follows the Senator's appeal'), the request was conditional ('approve any request'), and the dominant purpose of the release is pressing pending legislation. This was the most ambiguous call; the weak, inexplicit causal framing and the release's advocacy focus drove the 0."
  },
  "2368": {
    "document_id": "2368",
    "label": "1",
    "explanation": "Craig announces a concrete delivered benefit for Idaho constituents: the VA will expand Lewiston clinic services to five days per week with added mental health services. He also links the decision to his own advocacy, thanking officials 'for their willingness to hear my concerns and\u2014more importantly\u2014respond to the needs of the veterans.' This fits clarification (1) (announcing a federal benefit flowing to the state, which associates the senator with its delivery) and (4) (an agency decision following his intervention)."
  },
  "2382": {
    "document_id": "2382",
    "label": "1",
    "explanation": "Although the release primarily concerns a newly introduced bill (which alone would not qualify under the negative clarification on introducing legislation), it contains a substantive passage asserting a delivered result from Landrieu's personal intervention: 'By intervening with the Department of Homeland Security and removing bureaucratic red tape, Sen. Landrieu recently ensured that Rayan, a little girl from Iraq with life-threatening birth defects, was able to come... to the United States for treatment.' This fits clarification (4) (advocacy producing a concrete result) and (5) (a passage touting a delivered benefit even when packaged with a new proposal)."
  },
  "2697": {
    "document_id": "2697",
    "label": "1",
    "explanation": "Inouye announces $225,000 in federal funding for coqui frog control on the Big Island and explicitly claims personal responsibility: after OMB denied the request, 'I then went looking and found another federal funding source to at least begin the control and containment process.' This fits clarification (1) (announcing federal funds flowing to the state) and (2) (explicit claim of responsibility for securing the funds), mirroring the Talent positive example."
  },
  "2827": {
    "document_id": "2827",
    "label": "0",
    "explanation": "This is a Lieberman op-ed arguing for continued commitment to the Iraq war and praising President Bush's steadfastness. It is a statement of issue positions with no announcement of any governmental benefit and no claim of responsibility for a delivered outcome, excluded under the negative clarification ('statements of issue positions')."
  },
  "2895": {
    "document_id": "2895",
    "label": "1",
    "explanation": "The release announces Senate passage of the Improving America's Security Act and claims McCaskill's amendment was included: 'The bill also contains McCaskill's amendment to provide whistleblower protection and collective bargaining rights for airport screeners.' It also notes Missouri stands to receive an estimated $26.5 million. Clarification (3) expressly includes claims that the senator's amendment was adopted or that their bill passed at any stage, and clarification (1) covers announcing funds flowing to the state."
  },
  "3038": {
    "document_id": "3038",
    "label": "0",
    "explanation": "Snowe's release is a hearing statement supporting Vice Admiral Allen's nomination to be Coast Guard Commandant, praising Allen and outgoing Commandant Collins. It announces no benefit delivered to Maine or any constituency and claims no role in producing any outcome; it is a statement of support at a hearing (event/position statement), which the negative clarification treats as non-credit-claiming ('statements of issue positions,' 'announcements of... hearings')."
  },
  "3143": {
    "document_id": "3143",
    "label": "1",
    "explanation": "The release announces Senate passage of the Farm Bill and claims Graham's provisions were included: 'Graham worked to include additional grant programs that could benefit research and training... in South Carolina' and 'The legislation also includes a Graham-backed provision that would provide economic adjustment assistance... to textile manufacturers.' A state official also thanks Graham for 'securing passage of the Senate Bill.' This fits clarification (3) (claims that the senator's provisions were adopted or included in legislation that passed at any stage) and (2) (explicit responsibility claims)."
  },
  "3149": {
    "document_id": "3149",
    "label": "1",
    "explanation": "The release announces Senate passage of the FY2008 budget resolution and claims Reed's personal imprint on it: 'A provision championed by Reed to help establish an affordable housing fund financed by government sponsored enterprises.' Asserting that a provision he championed was included in legislation that just passed fits clarification (3) (claims that the senator's provision was adopted or their language included in legislation) and (2) (explicit responsibility claims for a specific outcome). The future-oriented portions (e.g., 'I will be proposing legislation') do not negate the credit claim embedded in the passed budget."
  },
  "3817": {
    "document_id": "3817",
    "label": "0",
    "explanation": "Sessions applauds the TVA Board's vote to submit a license application for Bellefonte. He claims no causal role\u2014he says only that the issue 'has been a priority of mine' and 'I applaud the Board,' which the negative clarification expressly excludes ('merely applauding, welcoming, or commenting on another actor's decision without claiming a causal role'; general 'lists of priorities'). Moreover, the Board's action is only a decision to apply, not a delivered benefit."
  },
  "4328": {
    "document_id": "4328",
    "label": "1",
    "explanation": "Alexander and Corker announce that the Department of Transportation has decided to support non-stop Jackson\u2013Cincinnati air service through the Essential Air Service program\u2014a delivered federal benefit for Tennessee\u2014and note that they 'wrote a letter in support of Jackson's application.' This fits clarification (1) (announcing a federal benefit flowing to the state associates the senators with its delivery) and (4) (an agency decision following their advocacy), paralleling the Lott positive example where FEMA action followed the senator's appeal."
  },
  "4403": {
    "document_id": "4403",
    "label": "1",
    "explanation": "Although cosponsoring the newly introduced R-HoPE Act alone would not qualify, the release contains substantive passages touting Domenici's enacted legislative record: it states the bill extends 'provisions\u2014included in the MMA that Domenici first authored and offered as legislation in February 2003\u2014to put rural physicians more on par with urban doctors in terms of Medicare reimbursement.' This asserts his authorship of provisions actually enacted in the Medicare Modernization Act that deliver benefits to rural New Mexico providers, fitting clarification (5) (passages touting the senator's record of enacted legislation benefiting a constituency, even when packaged with a new proposal) and (3)."
  }
}
